## Running Locally

Prerequisites: Bun ≥1.0, Postgres, Redis, an Ethereum RPC URL.

```bash
cp .env.example .env   # fill DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, RPC_URL, PONDER_URL, etc.

# 1. Start Postgres & Redis locally (or point to cloud services)

# 2. Fire up every dev service (API + worker + indexer) at once
bun run dev           # concurrently runs dev:api, dev:worker, dev:ponder

#    — or — start them individually in separate terminals
bun run dev:api       # Elysia HTTP API (Swagger: http://localhost:3000/swagger)
bun run dev:worker    # BullMQ confirmation & finalization workers (concurrently)
bun run dev:ponder    # Ponder blockchain indexer (GraphQL: http://localhost:42069/graphql)

# 3. Start the poller that bridges indexed events to the API (needs CHAIN_ID & PONDER_URL)
bun run src/poller.ts
```

Everything is hot-reloading (thanks to Bun's `--watch` and Ponder dev). Transactions to the foundation wallet should propagate through the pipeline automatically.

