## Precision-Safety

All monetary amounts are stored as `bigint` (base-units) in Postgres and handled in-memory with `Decimal.js` helpers (`toBigInt`, `fromBigInt`, `customToFixed`). No `Number` casts are used in critical paths, eliminating floating-point precision loss.

---

## Reliability & Chain Re-org Handling

Main-net Ethereum occasionally reorganises a few blocks or your local indexer might restart mid-block. The system combines three layers of protection so **no transfer is ever lost**:

1. **Confirmation depth** – The poller always keeps its cursor two blocks _behind_ the highest block it saw. Each run re-reads those two blocks, so extra transfers inserted later (or rewritten after a small re-org) are processed on the next cycle.
2. **Idempotent inserts** – All `INSERT` statements in the indexer, poller and confirmation code paths include `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING/UPDATE`. Re-processing the same event simply skips the duplicate row; no crash, no data loss.
3. **Retryable failure logging** – `confirm-purchase.ts` categorises failures and writes them to `failed_operations`. Retryable ones are automatically re-queued by BullMQ.

The worst case during a crash or re-org is a **duplicate insert attempt** that Postgres skips via `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`. No extra rows are created and no USDC → GCTL purchase can slip through the cracks.

